ine-height:100%">Mark Maughan</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:5.2pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%;position:relative;top:-2.8pt;vertical-align:baseline">(7)</span></div><div style="padding-left:9pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Former Chief Operating Officer</span></div></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">2026</span></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">326,859</span></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">-</span></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">1,748,522</span></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">-</span></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">2,546,426</span></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">4,621,807</span></td></tr></table></div><div style="margin-top:9pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(1)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;In May 2025, the compensation committee approved a $300,000 cash bonus for Mr. Thayne, that was paid in three tranches during fiscal 2026, based on his continued employment.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(2)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;The amounts reported in this column represent the aggregate grant date fair value of the restricted stock units, or RSUs, granted under our Plan to our named executive officers in each of the fiscal years ended January 31, 2026, 2025 and 2024 as computed in accordance with FASB ASC Topic 718. The assumptions used in calculating the dollar amount recognized for financial statement reporting purposes of the equity awards reported in this column are set forth in the notes to our financial statements included in our annual report on Form 10-K for the fiscal year ended January 31, 2026. Note that the amounts reported in this column reflect the accounting value for these equity awards and do not correspond to the actual economic value that may be received by our named executive officers from the equity awards.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(3)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;The amounts reported in this column for 2026 represent amounts earned and payable under the Executive Incentive Compensation Plan, or the Bonus Plan, for the fiscal year ended January 31, 2026, which we currently plan to satisfy with grants of fully-vested RSUs in the second quarter of fiscal 2027.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(4)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;The dollar amounts in this column include:</span></div><div style="padding-left:72pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:110%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:110%;padding-left:13.8pt">Company-paid matching 401(k) contributions of $14,000 each for Messrs. James, Thayne and Crane and $13,074 for Mr. Maughan.</span></div><div style="padding-left:72pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%;padding-left:13.8pt">Tax gross-ups for meal reimbursements of $1,245, $941 and $1,463 for Messrs. Thayne, Crane and Maughan, respectively.</span></div><div style="padding-left:72pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%;padding-left:13.8pt">For Mr. Maughan, $1,500,000 in cash and $995,599 in value from the accelerated vesting of his outstanding RSUs pursuant to a separation and settlement agreement and mutual release and $36,290 in post-employment consulting fees. The grant date fair value of the 125,000 fully-vested RSUs pursuant to the separation and settlement agreement and mutual release are included in Stock Awards for Mr. Maughan.</span></div><div style="margin-top:6pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(5)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Mr. James served as our principal executive officer until December 4, 2025, on which date he reduced his duties to focus on his health while continuing to serve as our Chief Executive Officer. Effective December 4, 2025, Mr. Thayne was appointed interim principal executive officer. Mr. James resumed serving as our principal executive officer effective April 15, 2026, and Mr. Thayne simultaneously ceased service as interim principal executive officer.</span></div><div style="margin-top:6pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(6)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Mr. Crane was appointed as our Chief Financial Officer effective November 1, 2024. Prior to his appointment, Mr. Crane was not a named executive officer of our company.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(7)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Mr. Maughan served as our Chief Operating Officer from March 14, 2025 until his resignation on January 11, 2026. Prior to his appointment, Mr. Maughan was not a named executive officer of our company. </span></div><div style="height:72pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-20.25pt"><span><br/></span></div></div></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:72pt;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div><div style="margin-top:12pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:145%">Grants of Plan-Based Awards for Fiscal Year Ended January 31, 2026</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:10pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">The following table sets forth information concerning grants of plan-based awards made during the fiscal year ended January 31, 2026 to each of our named executive officers.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:6pt"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:6.752%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:9.156%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:13.643%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:7.714%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:5.630%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:7.714%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:7.714%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:5.791%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:7.714%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:8.355%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:7.717%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/></tr><tr style="height:57pt"><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" rowspan="2" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><div style="margin-top:2.65pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%">&#160;</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:1.5pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%">Grant Date</span></div></