#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">*</span></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><div><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:700;line-height:100%">All Executive Officers &amp; Directors as a Group (12 persons)</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:5.85pt;font-weight:700;line-height:100%;position:relative;top:-3.15pt;vertical-align:baseline">(18)</span></div></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">3,263,659</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">100%</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">2,717,702</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">&#160;</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">6.4</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">&#160;</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">77.2</span></td></tr></table></div><div style="margin-top:9pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">*&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Represents beneficial ownership or voting power of less than 1%.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(1)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Percentage of total voting power represents voting power with respect to all outstanding shares of our Class A common stock and our Class B common stock, voting as a single class. Each holder of our Class A common stock shall be entitled to 40 votes per share of Class A common stock and each holder of our Class B common stock shall be entitled to one vote per share of Class B common stock. Holders of our Class A common stock and our Class B common stock will vote together as a single class on all matters (including the election of directors) submitted to a vote of stockholders, unless otherwise required by law or the Charter. The Class A common stock is convertible at any time by the holder into shares of Class B common stock on a share-for-share basis.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(2)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Based solely on a Schedule 13G/A filed with the SEC on February 7, 2025, BlackRock, Inc. is deemed to beneficially own 2,439,099 shares of our Class B common stock, with sole dispositive power as to 2,439,099 shares and sole voting power as to 2,422,014 shares. The address for BlackRock, Inc. is 50 Hudson Yards, New York, NY 10001.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(3)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Based solely on a Schedule 13G filed with the SEC on April 15, 2025, BlackRock Portfolio Management LLC is deemed to beneficially own 1,938,680 shares of our Class B common stock, with sole dispositive power as to 1,938,680 shares and sole voting power as to 1,896,278 shares. The address for BlackRock Portfolio Management LLC is 50 Hudson Yards, New York, NY 10001.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(4)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Based solely on a Schedule 13D filed with the SEC on March 9, 2026 by RPD Fund Management LLC (&#8220;RPD Management&#8221;), RPD Opportunity LLC (&#8220;RPD Opportunity&#8221;), RPD Opportunity Fund LP (&#8220;RPD Fund&#8221;) and Ahmet H. Okumus (collectively, the &#8220;RPD Entities&#8221;). RPD Management is the investment manager of RPD Fund, and RPD Opportunity is the general partner of RPD Fund. RPD Management and Ahmet H. Okumus are deemed to beneficially own 4,613,726 shares of our Class B common stock, with shared dispositive power as to 4,613,726 shares and shared voting power as to 4,613,726 shares. RPD Opportunity and RPD Fund are deemed to beneficially own 3,512,826 shares of our Class B common stock, with shared dispositive power as to 3,512,826 shares and shared voting power as to 3,512,826 shares. Each of the RPD Entities disclaim beneficial ownership of the reported securities except to the extent </span></div><div style="height:72pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:72pt;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">of their pecuniary interest therein. The address of each of the RPD Entities is 599 Lexington Avenue Suite 4700, New York, NY 10022..</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(5)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Based solely on a Schedule 13G filed with the SEC on April 29, 2026, Vanguard Portfolio Management is deemed to beneficially own 3,250,380 shares of our Class B common stock, with sole dispositive power as to 3,250,380 shares and sole voting power as to 27,641 shares. The address for Vanguard Portfolio Management and its affiliated entities is 100 Vanguard Blvd., Malvern, PA 19355.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(6)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Mr. James holds sole dispositive power and sole voting power over 4,458,779 shares of our Class A and Class B common stock, consisting of (a) 3,263,659 shares of our Class A common stock and 429,810 shares of our Class B common stock held of record by Cocolalla, LLC, (b) 561,567 shares of our Class B common stock held of record by Mr. James, (c) RSUs representing the right to receive 75,000 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026, (d) 10,000 shares of our Class B common stock held of record by Cinnamon Birch, LLC, (e) 116,600 shares of our Class B common stock held by the James Family Charitable Remainder Trust, and (f) 2,143 shares of our Class B common stock held of record by Mr. James&#8217; spouse. Mr. James is the manager of each of Cocolalla, LLC and Cinnamon Birch, LLC with voting and dispositive power over the shares held by Cocolalla, LLC and Cinnamon Birch, LLC. The address for Cocolalla, LLC, Cinnamon Birch, LLC and Mr. James is 550 Timpanogos Circle, Orem, UT 84097.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(7)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 74,533 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Crane and (b) RSUs representing the right to receive 27,500 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(8)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 272,368 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Thayne, (b) 103,552 shares of our Class B common stock held of record by Daren and Sharisa Thayne Family, LLC (over which Mr. Thayne has voting and dispositive power), and (c) RSUs representing the right to receive 34,375 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026.   </span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(9)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 296,489 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Maughan and (b) 1,167 shares of our Class B common stock issuable upon exercise of options issued to Mr. Maughan that are exercisable within 60 days of May 22, 2026.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(10)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 59,898 shares of our Class B common stock held by Ms. Clark and (b) RSUs representing the right to receive 13,461 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(11)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 58,981 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Daniel, (b) 8,420 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Daniel&#8217;s spouse, and (c) RSUs held by Mr. Daniel representing the right to receive 13,461 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(12)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 67,136 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Kearl, (b) 2,348 shares of our Class B common stock held of record by Pura Vida Investment Capital LLC, and (c) RSUs representing the right to receive 13,461 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026. Mr. Kearl exercises voting and dispositive control over the shares of our Class B common stock held by Pura Vida Investment Capital LLC.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(13)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 48,309 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Pestana, (b) 96,490 shares of our Class B common stock held of record by Erutinmo LLC, and (c) RSUs representing the right to receive 13,461 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026. Mr. Pestana exercises voting and dispositive control over the shares of our Class B common stock held by Erutinmo LLC.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(14)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 54,226 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Strong and (b) RSUs representing the right to receive 13,461 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(15)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 54,226 shares of our Class B common stock held by Ms. Soto and (b) RSUs representing the right to receive 13,461 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(16)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 133,022 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Jolley and (b) RSUs representing the right to receive 25,167 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(17)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 16,879 shares of our Class B common stock held by Mr. Wright and (b) RSUs representing the right to receive 6,730 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026.</span></div><div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">(18)&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Consists of (a) 2,658,128 shares of our Class B common stock directly or indirectly held by our directors and current executive officers, (b) options to purchase 1,167 shares of our Class B common stock that are exercisable within 60 days of May 22, 2026 and (c) RSUs representing the right to receive 249,538 shares of our Class B common stock scheduled to vest within 60 days of May 22, 2026.</span></div><div style="height:72pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div></div><div id="ief1ac10b9e5b47e69d2b426d5dd87ba1_40"></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:72pt;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:145%">RELATED-PERSON TRANSACTIONS</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">The following is a summary of transactions since February 1, 2025 to which we have been a party in which the amount involved exceeded $120,000 and in which any of our executive officers, directors, promoters or beneficial holders of more than 5% of our capital stock had or will have a direct or indirect material interest, other than compensation arrangements which are described under the section of this proxy statement entitled &#8220;Executive Compensation.&#8221;</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:145%">Related-Person Transactions Policy</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">We have adopted a formal, written policy that our executive officers, directors (including director nominees), holders of more than 5% of any class of our voting securities and any member of the immediate family of or any entities affiliated with any of the foregoing persons, are not permitted to enter into a related-person transaction with us without the prior approval or, in the case of pending or ongoing related party transactions, ratification of our audit committee. For purposes of our policy, a related-person transaction is a transaction, arrangement or relationship where we were, are or will be involved and in which a related party had, has or will have a direct or indirect material interest.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">Certain transactions with related-person, however, are excluded from the definition of a related-person transaction including, but not limited to:</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%;padding-left:14.5pt">transactions involving the purchase or sale of products or services in the ordinary course of business, not exceeding $120,000; </span></div><div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%;padding-left:14.5pt">transactions where a related-person&#8217;s interest derives solely from their service as a director of another entity that is a party to the transaction; </span></div><div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%;padding-left:14.5pt">transactions where a related-person&#8217;s interest derives solely from their ownership of less than 10% of the equity interest in another entity that is a party to the transaction; and </span></div><div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%;padding-left:14.5pt">transactions where a related-person&#8217;s interest derives solely from their ownership of a class of our equity securities and all holders of that class received the same benefit on a pro rata basis.</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">No member of the audit committee may participate in any review, consideration or approval of any related party transaction where such member or any of their immediate family members is the related-person. In approving or rejecting the proposed agreement, our audit committee shall consider the relevant facts and circumstances available and deemed relevant to the audit committee, including, but not limited to:</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%;padding-left:14.5pt">the benefits and perceived benefits to us; </span></div><div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%;padding-left:14.5pt">the materiality and character of the related-person&#8217;s direct and indirect interest; </span></div><div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%;padding-left:14.5pt">the availability of other sources for comparable products or services; </span></div><div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%;padding-left:14.5pt">the terms of the transaction; and </span></div><div style="margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">&#8226;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%;padding-left:14.5pt">the terms available to unrelated third parties under the same or similar circumstances.</span></div><div style="height:72pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:72pt;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">In reviewing proposed related-person transactions, the audit committee will only approve or ratify related person transactions that are in, or not inconsistent with, the best interests of us and our stockholders.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">Registration Rights Agreement</span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">On March 1, 2022, we entered into a registration rights agreement (the &#8220;Registration Rights Agreement&#8221;) with Mr. James, our Founder, CEO and member of our board of directors, pursuant to which Mr. James has the right to require us to register the offer and sale of shares of Class A common stock (including shares of Class A common stock issued upon conversion of Class B common stock) held by Mr. James or his affiliates (such rights are referred to as &#8220;registration rights&#8221;).</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">Mr. James has the right to demand that we use best efforts to file a registration statement for the registration of the offer and sale of at least that number of shares with anticipated offering proceeds in excess of $20.0 million. We are only obligated to file up to two registration statements in connection with the exercise of demand registration rights. These registration rights are subject to specified conditions and limitations, including our ability to defer the filing of a registration statement with respect to an exercise of such demand registration rights for up to 90 days under certain circumstances.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">At any time that we are eligible to use a registration statement on Form S-3, Mr. James has the right to demand that we file a registration statement on Form S-3 so long as the aggregate number of shares to be offered and sold under such registration statement on Form S-3 is at least $5.0 million. We are only obligated to file one registration statement in connection with the exercise of such Form S-3 registration rights. These registration rights are subject to specified conditions and limitations, including our ability to defer the filing of a registration statement with respect to an exercise of such Form S-3 registration rights for up to 90 days under certain circumstances.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">If we propose to register the offer and sale of any of our securities under the Securities Act, either for our own account or for the account of other stockholders, Mr. James has the right, subject to certain exceptions, to include his registrable shares in the registration statement. We are only obligated to register shares in connection with Mr. James&#8217; exercise of these piggyback registration rights with respect to one registration. This registration right is subject to specified conditions and limitations, including the right of the underwriters to limit the number of shares included in any such registration statement under certain circumstances.</span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">The registration rights will terminate on March 1, 2027.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"><br/></span></div><div><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Employees and Consultants</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">During the fiscal year ended January&#160;31, 2026, we paid to LATAM-AS-A-SERVICE, LLC, a company controlled by Luis Bardin, Mr. James&#8217; father-in-law, approximately $254,386 for sales services. Effective March 15, 2026, this consulting arrangement was terminated and Mr. Bardin was hired as an employee of the Company, effective March 1, 2026, with a base salary of approximately $150,000. Mr. Bardin is also eligible to participate in sales incentive bonuses and our health and other benefit plans as well as our employee stock purchase plan, in each case on terms and conditions applicable to similarly situated employees.</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">During the fiscal year ended January&#160;31, 2026, we employed Denise Daniel, the spouse of Daniel Daniel, in a non-executive employee position. Compensation received by Ms. Daniel for fiscal 2026 included a base salary of approximately $120,000 and 5,111 restricted stock units. Ms. Daniel also participated in our health and other benefit </span></div><div style="height:72pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:72pt;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">plans as well as our employee stock purchase plan, in each case on terms and conditions applicable to similarly situated employees.</span></div><div style="text-align:justify"><span><br/></span></div><div><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Donations</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">During the fiscal year ended January&#160;31, 2026, we donated $50,000 to Silicon Slopes, a non-profit organization. Mr. James is on the board of directors of Silicon Slopes.</span></div><div><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Other</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">We have entered into agreements with certain of our executive officers that, among other things, provide for certain severance and change of control benefits. For a description of these agreements, see section entitled &#8220;Executive Compensation&#8212;Executive Employment Arrangements.&#8221;</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">We have entered into indemnification agreements with our directors and executive officers.</span></div><div style="height:72pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div></div><div id="ief1ac10b9e5b47e69d2b426d5dd87ba1_43"></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:72pt;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:145%">OTHER MATTERS</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:10pt;margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:145%">Third Party Compensation of Directors</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">None of our directors are a party to any agreement or arrangement that would require disclosure pursuant to&#160;Rule 5250(b)(3) of The Nasdaq Stock Market.</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:145%">Delinquent Section 16(a) Reports</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">Section 16(a) of the Exchange Act requires our directors and executive officers, and persons who own more than ten percent of a registered class of our equity securities, to file reports of ownership and changes in ownership with the SEC. Based solely on our review of Forms 3, 4 and 5 and amendments thereto filed electronically with the SEC by the reporting persons, and written representations from certain reporting persons, we believe that during the fiscal year ended January 31, 2025, our directors, executive officers, and ten percent stockholders complied with all Section 16(a) filing requirements applicable to them, except: (i) Forms 4 relating to reportable restricted stock unit grants due on May 29, 2025, but filed by Messrs. Thayne, Crane and Maughan on June 16, 2025, due to administrative errors; and (ii) Forms 3 and 4 relating to Mr. Wright's appointment to our board and his reportable initial restricted stock grant due on March 17, 2025 and March 10, 2025, respectively, but filed by Mr. Wright on March 18, 2025, due to an unanticipated delay in obtaining his EDGAR filing codes.</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:145%">2026 Annual Report and SEC Filings</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-right:6.75pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">Our financial statements for the fiscal year ended January&#160;31, 2026 are included in our annual report on Form 10-K. Links to our annual report and this proxy statement can be found under Financials at http://www.domoinvestors.com. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:145%">You may also obtain a copy of our annual report without charge by sending a written request to Investor Relations, Domo, Inc., 802 East 1050 South, American Fork, UT 84003.</span></div><div style="padding-right:6.75pt;text-align:justify"><span><br/></span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;text-align:center"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">*   *   *</span></div><div style="text-align:center"><span><br/></span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-right:6.75pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">The board of directors does not know of any other matters to be presented at the Annual Meeting. If any additional matters are properly presented at the Annual Meeting, the persons named in the enclosed proxy card will have discretion to vote shares they represent in accordance with their own judgment on such matters.</span></div><div style="height:72pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div><span><br/></span></div></div></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"/><div style="min-height:72pt;width:100%"><div style="padding-right:-18pt"><span><br/></span></div></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-right:6.75pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:145%">It is important that your shares be represented at the Annual Meeting, regardless of the number of shares that you hold. You are, therefore, urged to vote by using the internet or telephone as instructed in the Notice or on the enclosed proxy card, or by executing and returning by mail, at your earliest convenience, the enclosed proxy card in the envelope that has also been provided (if you received printed proxy materials).</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt"><span><br/></span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:245.25pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:145%">THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS</span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt"><span><br/></span></div><div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:245.25pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size: